{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.edf953251e","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-c-366","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Pembrook Observatory is in southern New Zealand. It began operating in 1905.</li><li>Its main telescope's mirror diameter is 10 meters.</li><li>The Orla Observatory is in western Kenya. It began operating in 1926.</li><li>Its main telescope's mirror diameter is 8 meters.</li><li>Both are radio observatories.</li></ul><p>The student wants to emphasize how the main telescope's mirror diameter of the two observatorys differs.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The main telescope's mirror diameter of the Pembrook Observatory (10 meters) is greater than that of the Orla Observatory (8 meters).","Both the Pembrook Observatory and the Orla Observatory are radio observatories.","The Pembrook Observatory began operating in 1905, while the Orla Observatory began operating in 1926.","The Pembrook Observatory, which is in southern New Zealand, is one of several radio observatories."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It compares the main telescope's mirror diameter of both observatorys. The other choices describe a similarity, a difference in date, or only one observatory."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.b75d96e1d5","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-c-369","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Valewood National Park is in eastern Poland. It was established in 1978.</li><li>Its area is 8,644 square kilometers.</li><li>Thornbury National Park is in southern New Zealand. It was established in 1894.</li><li>Its area is 5,011 square kilometers.</li><li>Both are parks known for their old-growth forests.</li></ul><p>The student wants to emphasize how the area of the two parks differs.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Both Valewood National Park and Thornbury National Park are parks known for their old-growth forests.","Valewood National Park was established in 1978, while Thornbury National Park was established in 1894.","Valewood National Park, which is in eastern Poland, is one of several parks known for their old-growth forests.","The area of Valewood National Park (8,644 square kilometers) is greater than that of Thornbury National Park (5,011 square kilometers)."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It compares the area of both parks. The other choices describe a similarity, a difference in date, or only one park."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.c3fc0afe36","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-c-373","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Lake Cresthill is in southern Norway. It was first surveyed in 1932.</li><li>Its surface area is 560 square kilometers.</li><li>Lake Larkspur is in southern New Zealand. It was first surveyed in 1976.</li><li>Its surface area is 389 square kilometers.</li><li>Both are freshwater lakes formed by glaciers.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast when the two lakes were first surveyed.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Lake Cresthill was first surveyed in 1932, while Lake Larkspur was first surveyed in 1976.","Both Lake Cresthill and Lake Larkspur are freshwater lakes formed by glaciers.","Lake Cresthill is in southern Norway, and Lake Larkspur is in southern New Zealand.","The surface area of Lake Cresthill (560 square kilometers) is greater than that of Lake Larkspur (389 square kilometers)."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It gives both dates and contrasts them. The other choices compare size or location, or describe a similarity."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.8938aa6cf4","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-c-379","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Pembrook Museum is in western Kenya. It opened in 1930.</li><li>Its annual attendance is 864,230 visitors.</li><li>The Redfern Museum is in southern Norway. It opened in 1994.</li><li>Its annual attendance is 703,803 visitors.</li><li>Both are museums of natural history.</li></ul><p>The student wants to emphasize how the annual attendance of the two museums differs.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Both the Pembrook Museum and the Redfern Museum are museums of natural history.","The Pembrook Museum opened in 1930, while the Redfern Museum opened in 1994.","The Pembrook Museum, which is in western Kenya, is one of several museums of natural history.","The annual attendance of the Pembrook Museum (864,230 visitors) is greater than that of the Redfern Museum (703,803 visitors)."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It compares the annual attendance of both museums. The other choices describe a similarity, a difference in date, or only one museum."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.6b345f7080","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-c-383","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Mount Eastwick is in northern Chile. It was first climbed in 1927.</li><li>Its height is 6,300 meters.</li><li>Mount Juniper is in northern Japan. It was first climbed in 2015.</li><li>Its height is 3,816 meters.</li><li>Both are peaks in the same mountain range.</li></ul><p>The student wants to emphasize a similarity between Mount Eastwick and Mount Juniper.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Mount Eastwick was first climbed in 1927, while Mount Juniper was first climbed in 2015.","Mount Eastwick is in northern Chile, and Mount Juniper is in northern Japan.","Both Mount Eastwick and Mount Juniper are peaks in the same mountain range.","The height of Mount Eastwick (6,300 meters) is greater than that of Mount Juniper (3,816 meters)."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. Only this choice describes something the two share. The others present differences (in size, date, or location)."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.80b56e6140","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-c-389","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Redfern Bridge is in southern New Zealand. It opened in 1984.</li><li>Its main span is 1,583 meters.</li><li>The Northam Bridge is in eastern Poland. It opened in 1921.</li><li>Its main span is 1,528 meters.</li><li>Both are suspension bridges.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast when the two bridges opened.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Redfern Bridge opened in 1984, while the Northam Bridge opened in 1921.","The Redfern Bridge is in southern New Zealand, and the Northam Bridge is in eastern Poland.","Both the Redfern Bridge and the Northam Bridge are suspension bridges.","The main span of the Redfern Bridge (1,583 meters) is greater than that of the Northam Bridge (1,528 meters)."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It gives both dates and contrasts them. The other choices compare size or location, or describe a similarity."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.18421f0546","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-c-390","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Valewood Tunnel is in southern Norway. It opened in 1999.</li><li>Its length is 11 kilometers.</li><li>The Eastwick Tunnel is in southern New Zealand. It opened in 2011.</li><li>Its length is 5 kilometers.</li><li>Both are railway tunnels.</li></ul><p>The student wants to emphasize how the length of the two tunnels differs.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Valewood Tunnel opened in 1999, while the Eastwick Tunnel opened in 2011.","Both the Valewood Tunnel and the Eastwick Tunnel are railway tunnels.","The Valewood Tunnel, which is in southern Norway, is one of several railway tunnels.","The length of the Valewood Tunnel (11 kilometers) is greater than that of the Eastwick Tunnel (5 kilometers)."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It compares the length of both tunnels. The other choices describe a similarity, a difference in date, or only one tunnel."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.a4fe35f053","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-c-394","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Lake Halden is in eastern Poland. It was first surveyed in 1911.</li><li>Its surface area is 854 square kilometers.</li><li>Lake Dunmore is in central Spain. It was first surveyed in 1978.</li><li>Its surface area is 658 square kilometers.</li><li>Both are reservoirs created by dams.</li></ul><p>The student wants to emphasize a similarity between Lake Halden and Lake Dunmore.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Lake Halden was first surveyed in 1911, while Lake Dunmore was first surveyed in 1978.","The surface area of Lake Halden (854 square kilometers) is greater than that of Lake Dunmore (658 square kilometers).","Lake Halden is in eastern Poland, and Lake Dunmore is in central Spain.","Both Lake Halden and Lake Dunmore are reservoirs created by dams."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. Only this choice describes something the two share. The others present differences (in size, date, or location)."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.041327401b","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-c-398","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Glenrock Tunnel is in southern Norway. It opened in 1913.</li><li>Its length is 22 kilometers.</li><li>The Brookhaven Tunnel is in southern Brazil. It opened in 1974.</li><li>Its length is 14 kilometers.</li><li>Both are tunnels that pass under a mountain range.</li></ul><p>The student wants to emphasize a similarity between the Glenrock Tunnel and the Brookhaven Tunnel.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Glenrock Tunnel opened in 1913, while the Brookhaven Tunnel opened in 1974.","The Glenrock Tunnel is in southern Norway, and the Brookhaven Tunnel is in southern Brazil.","Both the Glenrock Tunnel and the Brookhaven Tunnel are tunnels that pass under a mountain range.","The length of the Glenrock Tunnel (22 kilometers) is greater than that of the Brookhaven Tunnel (14 kilometers)."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. Only this choice describes something the two share. The others present differences (in size, date, or location)."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.e8654c0222","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-6","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Sofia Halvorsen is an ecologist.</li><li>Halvorsen wanted to find out whether city lights change when songbirds begin singing in the morning.</li><li>Halvorsen compared the first songs of robins in brightly lit city parks with those in dark rural woodlands.</li><li>Halvorsen found that robins in lit parks began singing nearly an hour earlier.</li><li>Halvorsen concluded that artificial light may shift birds' daily rhythms.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Halvorsen compared the first songs of robins in brightly lit city parks with those in dark rural woodlands.","Ecologist Sofia Halvorsen set out to learn whether city lights change when songbirds begin singing in the morning.","Halvorsen found that robins in lit parks began singing nearly an hour earlier.","Halvorsen concluded that artificial light may shift birds' daily rhythms."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.5496ce797b","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-13","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Kofi Castellano is a psychologist.</li><li>Castellano wanted to find out whether taking short breaks improves students' focus during long study sessions.</li><li>Castellano had one group of students take a five-minute break every half hour while another group studied without breaks.</li><li>Castellano found that students who took breaks answered more practice questions correctly.</li><li>Castellano concluded that brief breaks may help people stay focused.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Castellano had one group of students take a five-minute break every half hour while another group studied without breaks.","Castellano concluded that brief breaks may help people stay focused.","Psychologist Kofi Castellano set out to learn whether taking short breaks improves students' focus during long study sessions.","Castellano found that students who took breaks answered more practice questions correctly."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.0110f865dd","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-16","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Felipe Haddad is a psychologist.</li><li>Haddad wanted to find out whether taking short breaks improves students' focus during long study sessions.</li><li>Haddad had one group of students take a five-minute break every half hour while another group studied without breaks.</li><li>Haddad found that students who took breaks answered more practice questions correctly.</li><li>Haddad concluded that brief breaks may help people stay focused.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Haddad found that students who took breaks answered more practice questions correctly.","Haddad concluded that brief breaks may help people stay focused.","To investigate the question, Haddad had one group of students take a five-minute break every half hour while another group studied without breaks.","Psychologist Felipe Haddad set out to learn whether taking short breaks improves students' focus during long study sessions."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.8084005ba6","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-26","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Kofi Moreau is a materials scientist.</li><li>Moreau wanted to find out whether a coating made from seaweed can keep fruit fresh longer.</li><li>Moreau coated half of a batch of strawberries with a seaweed-based film and left the rest uncoated.</li><li>Moreau found that coated strawberries stayed fresh for about four days longer.</li><li>Moreau concluded that the coating could help reduce food waste.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Moreau coated half of a batch of strawberries with a seaweed-based film and left the rest uncoated.","Moreau concluded that the coating could help reduce food waste.","Moreau found that coated strawberries stayed fresh for about four days longer.","Materials scientist Kofi Moreau set out to learn whether a coating made from seaweed can keep fruit fresh longer."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.c0aa21b5da","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-33","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Idris Solberg is an entomologist.</li><li>Solberg wanted to find out whether bees prefer flowers of a particular color.</li><li>Solberg set out identical feeders colored blue, yellow, and white in a meadow.</li><li>Solberg found that bees visited the blue feeders most often.</li><li>Solberg concluded that color may play a role in how bees choose flowers.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Solberg set out identical feeders colored blue, yellow, and white in a meadow.","Solberg found that bees visited the blue feeders most often.","Solberg concluded that color may play a role in how bees choose flowers.","Entomologist Idris Solberg set out to learn whether bees prefer flowers of a particular color."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.264a1db4dd","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-50","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ayumi Delacroix is a nutrition researcher.</li><li>Delacroix wanted to find out whether eating breakfast affects how much food people eat at lunch.</li><li>Delacroix asked volunteers to eat breakfast on some days and skip it on others, then measured their lunch portions.</li><li>Delacroix found that lunch portions were about the same on both kinds of days.</li><li>Delacroix concluded that skipping breakfast may not lead people to eat more later.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Delacroix concluded that skipping breakfast may not lead people to eat more later.","Delacroix found that lunch portions were about the same on both kinds of days.","Nutrition researcher Ayumi Delacroix set out to learn whether eating breakfast affects how much food people eat at lunch.","To investigate the question, Delacroix asked volunteers to eat breakfast on some days and skip it on others, then measured their lunch portions."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.49a06d1856","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-53","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Felipe Kowalski is a nutrition researcher.</li><li>Kowalski wanted to find out whether eating breakfast affects how much food people eat at lunch.</li><li>Kowalski asked volunteers to eat breakfast on some days and skip it on others, then measured their lunch portions.</li><li>Kowalski found that lunch portions were about the same on both kinds of days.</li><li>Kowalski concluded that skipping breakfast may not lead people to eat more later.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Nutrition researcher Felipe Kowalski set out to learn whether eating breakfast affects how much food people eat at lunch.","Kowalski concluded that skipping breakfast may not lead people to eat more later.","Kowalski found that lunch portions were about the same on both kinds of days.","To investigate the question, Kowalski asked volunteers to eat breakfast on some days and skip it on others, then measured their lunch portions."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.13cc4f407c","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-57","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Leila Kowalski is a zoologist.</li><li>Kowalski wanted to find out whether zoo elephants that are given puzzle feeders are more active.</li><li>Kowalski gave puzzle feeders to some elephants and standard food trays to others, then tracked their movement.</li><li>Kowalski found that elephants with puzzle feeders walked noticeably more each day.</li><li>Kowalski concluded that puzzle feeders may encourage healthy activity.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Zoologist Leila Kowalski set out to learn whether zoo elephants that are given puzzle feeders are more active.","To investigate the question, Kowalski gave puzzle feeders to some elephants and standard food trays to others, then tracked their movement.","Kowalski found that elephants with puzzle feeders walked noticeably more each day.","Kowalski concluded that puzzle feeders may encourage healthy activity."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.3b51b64ac9","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-60","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Kenji Delacroix is an astronomer.</li><li>Delacroix wanted to find out whether a distant star's brightness changes on a regular schedule.</li><li>Delacroix measured the star's brightness every night for eighteen months.</li><li>Delacroix found that the star dimmed slightly about every 42 days.</li><li>Delacroix concluded that an orbiting planet may be passing in front of the star.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Delacroix measured the star's brightness every night for eighteen months.","Astronomer Kenji Delacroix set out to learn whether a distant star's brightness changes on a regular schedule.","Delacroix found that the star dimmed slightly about every 42 days.","Delacroix concluded that an orbiting planet may be passing in front of the star."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.b81699d919","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-69","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Felipe Varga is a linguist.</li><li>Varga wanted to find out whether bilingual children are better at switching between tasks.</li><li>Varga gave bilingual and monolingual children a game that required switching rules quickly.</li><li>Varga found that bilingual children switched rules with fewer errors.</li><li>Varga concluded that speaking two languages may strengthen certain mental skills.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Varga found that bilingual children switched rules with fewer errors.","Varga concluded that speaking two languages may strengthen certain mental skills.","Linguist Felipe Varga set out to learn whether bilingual children are better at switching between tasks.","To investigate the question, Varga gave bilingual and monolingual children a game that required switching rules quickly."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.fb2775c7c4","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-79","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Lucía Vance is a botanist.</li><li>Vance wanted to find out whether tomato plants grow better with music played nearby.</li><li>Vance grew tomato plants in two identical greenhouses, one with music and one without.</li><li>Vance found that plants in both greenhouses grew at similar rates.</li><li>Vance concluded that music may have little effect on tomato growth.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Vance found that plants in both greenhouses grew at similar rates.","To investigate the question, Vance grew tomato plants in two identical greenhouses, one with music and one without.","Vance concluded that music may have little effect on tomato growth.","Botanist Lucía Vance set out to learn whether tomato plants grow better with music played nearby."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.d25e5e67b2","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-93","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Elias Sato is a hydrologist.</li><li>Sato wanted to find out whether wetlands reduce flooding downstream.</li><li>Sato compared river levels below restored wetlands with levels below drained farmland after storms.</li><li>Sato found that river levels rose more slowly below the wetlands.</li><li>Sato concluded that wetlands may help protect nearby communities from floods.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Hydrologist Elias Sato set out to learn whether wetlands reduce flooding downstream.","Sato found that river levels rose more slowly below the wetlands.","Sato concluded that wetlands may help protect nearby communities from floods.","To investigate the question, Sato compared river levels below restored wetlands with levels below drained farmland after storms."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.4d348dc9ec","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-97","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Sofia Quintero is an education researcher.</li><li>Quintero wanted to find out whether reading aloud to young children improves their vocabulary.</li><li>Quintero had parents in one group read aloud daily while another group continued their usual routines.</li><li>Quintero found that children in the read-aloud group learned more new words.</li><li>Quintero concluded that regular read-aloud time may support vocabulary growth.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Quintero found that children in the read-aloud group learned more new words.","To investigate the question, Quintero had parents in one group read aloud daily while another group continued their usual routines.","Quintero concluded that regular read-aloud time may support vocabulary growth.","Education researcher Sofia Quintero set out to learn whether reading aloud to young children improves their vocabulary."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.843ddd2a03","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-97","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Sofia Quintero is an education researcher.</li><li>Quintero wanted to find out whether reading aloud to young children improves their vocabulary.</li><li>Quintero had parents in one group read aloud daily while another group continued their usual routines.</li><li>Quintero found that children in the read-aloud group learned more new words.</li><li>Quintero concluded that regular read-aloud time may support vocabulary growth.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Quintero had parents in one group read aloud daily while another group continued their usual routines.","Education researcher Sofia Quintero set out to learn whether reading aloud to young children improves their vocabulary.","Quintero concluded that regular read-aloud time may support vocabulary growth.","Quintero found that children in the read-aloud group learned more new words."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.d38133aa91","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-101","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Jonas Oyelaran is an education researcher.</li><li>Oyelaran wanted to find out whether reading aloud to young children improves their vocabulary.</li><li>Oyelaran had parents in one group read aloud daily while another group continued their usual routines.</li><li>Oyelaran found that children in the read-aloud group learned more new words.</li><li>Oyelaran concluded that regular read-aloud time may support vocabulary growth.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Oyelaran found that children in the read-aloud group learned more new words.","To investigate the question, Oyelaran had parents in one group read aloud daily while another group continued their usual routines.","Education researcher Jonas Oyelaran set out to learn whether reading aloud to young children improves their vocabulary.","Oyelaran concluded that regular read-aloud time may support vocabulary growth."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.6ba648c97c","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-102","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Nadia Mbeki is a chemist.</li><li>Mbeki wanted to find out whether a new plant-based plastic breaks down in seawater.</li><li>Mbeki placed samples of the plastic in tanks of seawater for six months.</li><li>Mbeki found that most samples broke apart within four months.</li><li>Mbeki concluded that the plastic may be less harmful to oceans than conventional plastic.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Mbeki placed samples of the plastic in tanks of seawater for six months.","Mbeki found that most samples broke apart within four months.","Chemist Nadia Mbeki set out to learn whether a new plant-based plastic breaks down in seawater.","Mbeki concluded that the plastic may be less harmful to oceans than conventional plastic."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.fccc8c4686","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-107","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Diego Halvorsen is a chemist.</li><li>Halvorsen wanted to find out whether a new plant-based plastic breaks down in seawater.</li><li>Halvorsen placed samples of the plastic in tanks of seawater for six months.</li><li>Halvorsen found that most samples broke apart within four months.</li><li>Halvorsen concluded that the plastic may be less harmful to oceans than conventional plastic.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Halvorsen placed samples of the plastic in tanks of seawater for six months.","Halvorsen found that most samples broke apart within four months.","Halvorsen concluded that the plastic may be less harmful to oceans than conventional plastic.","Chemist Diego Halvorsen set out to learn whether a new plant-based plastic breaks down in seawater."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.ea6793d45c","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-120","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ravi Vance is an ornithologist.</li><li>Vance wanted to find out whether birds that migrate farther have longer wings.</li><li>Vance measured the wings of several related species with different migration distances.</li><li>Vance found that species that migrated farther tended to have longer, narrower wings.</li><li>Vance concluded that wing shape may be linked to migration distance.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Vance measured the wings of several related species with different migration distances.","Vance found that species that migrated farther tended to have longer, narrower wings.","Ornithologist Ravi Vance set out to learn whether birds that migrate farther have longer wings.","Vance concluded that wing shape may be linked to migration distance."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.974825c4ca","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-120","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ravi Vance is an ornithologist.</li><li>Vance wanted to find out whether birds that migrate farther have longer wings.</li><li>Vance measured the wings of several related species with different migration distances.</li><li>Vance found that species that migrated farther tended to have longer, narrower wings.</li><li>Vance concluded that wing shape may be linked to migration distance.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Ornithologist Ravi Vance set out to learn whether birds that migrate farther have longer wings.","Vance found that species that migrated farther tended to have longer, narrower wings.","To investigate the question, Vance measured the wings of several related species with different migration distances.","Vance concluded that wing shape may be linked to migration distance."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.78dec750b5","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-128","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Zara Moreau is a public health researcher.</li><li>Moreau wanted to find out whether adding bike lanes increases how often residents cycle.</li><li>Moreau counted cyclists on streets before and after new bike lanes were added.</li><li>Moreau found that cycling on those streets nearly doubled within a year.</li><li>Moreau concluded that bike lanes may encourage more people to ride.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Moreau concluded that bike lanes may encourage more people to ride.","Public health researcher Zara Moreau set out to learn whether adding bike lanes increases how often residents cycle.","Moreau found that cycling on those streets nearly doubled within a year.","To investigate the question, Moreau counted cyclists on streets before and after new bike lanes were added."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.3295f098b4","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-131","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Samuel Novak is a public health researcher.</li><li>Novak wanted to find out whether adding bike lanes increases how often residents cycle.</li><li>Novak counted cyclists on streets before and after new bike lanes were added.</li><li>Novak found that cycling on those streets nearly doubled within a year.</li><li>Novak concluded that bike lanes may encourage more people to ride.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Public health researcher Samuel Novak set out to learn whether adding bike lanes increases how often residents cycle.","Novak found that cycling on those streets nearly doubled within a year.","Novak concluded that bike lanes may encourage more people to ride.","To investigate the question, Novak counted cyclists on streets before and after new bike lanes were added."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.4547568ceb","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-133","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Viktor Takeda is an archaeologist.</li><li>Takeda wanted to find out whether a coastal settlement traded with inland villages.</li><li>Takeda analyzed the minerals in pottery found at the settlement.</li><li>Takeda found that many pots were made from clay found only far inland.</li><li>Takeda concluded that the settlement may have traded with inland communities.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Takeda concluded that the settlement may have traded with inland communities.","To investigate the question, Takeda analyzed the minerals in pottery found at the settlement.","Archaeologist Viktor Takeda set out to learn whether a coastal settlement traded with inland villages.","Takeda found that many pots were made from clay found only far inland."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.536cbad63a","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-140","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Hana Novak is a neuroscientist.</li><li>Novak wanted to find out whether learning to juggle changes brain structure.</li><li>Novak scanned volunteers' brains before and after three months of juggling practice.</li><li>Novak found that regions linked to tracking movement grew slightly larger.</li><li>Novak concluded that practicing a new skill may reshape parts of the brain.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Novak scanned volunteers' brains before and after three months of juggling practice.","Novak concluded that practicing a new skill may reshape parts of the brain.","Novak found that regions linked to tracking movement grew slightly larger.","Neuroscientist Hana Novak set out to learn whether learning to juggle changes brain structure."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.e78da248c1","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-142","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Zara Sato is a neuroscientist.</li><li>Sato wanted to find out whether learning to juggle changes brain structure.</li><li>Sato scanned volunteers' brains before and after three months of juggling practice.</li><li>Sato found that regions linked to tracking movement grew slightly larger.</li><li>Sato concluded that practicing a new skill may reshape parts of the brain.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Neuroscientist Zara Sato set out to learn whether learning to juggle changes brain structure.","Sato found that regions linked to tracking movement grew slightly larger.","To investigate the question, Sato scanned volunteers' brains before and after three months of juggling practice.","Sato concluded that practicing a new skill may reshape parts of the brain."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.edf6da2805","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-144","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ravi Castellano is a marine ecologist.</li><li>Castellano wanted to find out whether sea urchins limit the growth of kelp forests.</li><li>Castellano fenced urchins out of some kelp plots and left others open.</li><li>Castellano found that kelp in the fenced plots grew much denser.</li><li>Castellano concluded that urchins may keep kelp forests from expanding.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Marine ecologist Ravi Castellano set out to learn whether sea urchins limit the growth of kelp forests.","To investigate the question, Castellano fenced urchins out of some kelp plots and left others open.","Castellano concluded that urchins may keep kelp forests from expanding.","Castellano found that kelp in the fenced plots grew much denser."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.568e9c7531","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-148","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Kwame Ferreira is a marine ecologist.</li><li>Ferreira wanted to find out whether sea urchins limit the growth of kelp forests.</li><li>Ferreira fenced urchins out of some kelp plots and left others open.</li><li>Ferreira found that kelp in the fenced plots grew much denser.</li><li>Ferreira concluded that urchins may keep kelp forests from expanding.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Ferreira concluded that urchins may keep kelp forests from expanding.","To investigate the question, Ferreira fenced urchins out of some kelp plots and left others open.","Marine ecologist Kwame Ferreira set out to learn whether sea urchins limit the growth of kelp forests.","Ferreira found that kelp in the fenced plots grew much denser."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.c503064610","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-153","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Idris Nakamura is a climate scientist.</li><li>Nakamura wanted to find out whether light-colored roofs reduce indoor temperatures.</li><li>Nakamura compared indoor temperatures in homes with white roofs and homes with dark roofs.</li><li>Nakamura found that homes with white roofs stayed several degrees cooler.</li><li>Nakamura concluded that light-colored roofs may reduce the need for air-conditioning.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Nakamura found that homes with white roofs stayed several degrees cooler.","Climate scientist Idris Nakamura set out to learn whether light-colored roofs reduce indoor temperatures.","Nakamura concluded that light-colored roofs may reduce the need for air-conditioning.","To investigate the question, Nakamura compared indoor temperatures in homes with white roofs and homes with dark roofs."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.40798bfcee","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-167","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Priya Castellano is a veterinary scientist.</li><li>Castellano wanted to find out whether dogs recognize their owners' voices.</li><li>Castellano played recordings of owners' voices and strangers' voices to dogs.</li><li>Castellano found that dogs turned toward their owners' voices far more often.</li><li>Castellano concluded that dogs may be able to tell their owners' voices apart from others.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the study's finding.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Veterinary scientist Priya Castellano set out to learn whether dogs recognize their owners' voices.","Castellano concluded that dogs may be able to tell their owners' voices apart from others.","To investigate the question, Castellano played recordings of owners' voices and strangers' voices to dogs.","Castellano found that dogs turned toward their owners' voices far more often."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It reports what the researcher observed. A conclusion is an interpretation of a finding, not the finding itself."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.efb0d99aff","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-173","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Maren Iyer is a forest ecologist.</li><li>Iyer wanted to find out whether fungi help trees share nutrients.</li><li>Iyer added a traceable form of carbon to some trees and checked nearby trees for it.</li><li>Iyer found that the carbon appeared in neighboring trees connected by fungal networks.</li><li>Iyer concluded that fungal networks may move nutrients between trees.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Iyer found that the carbon appeared in neighboring trees connected by fungal networks.","To investigate the question, Iyer added a traceable form of carbon to some trees and checked nearby trees for it.","Forest ecologist Maren Iyer set out to learn whether fungi help trees share nutrients.","Iyer concluded that fungal networks may move nutrients between trees."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.2.31e6faa728","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":2,"group":"syn-s-179","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Beatriz Delacroix is a music researcher.</li><li>Delacroix wanted to find out whether learning an instrument improves children's listening skills.</li><li>Delacroix tested children's ability to pick out sounds in noise before and after two years of music lessons.</li><li>Delacroix found that children who took lessons improved more than those who did not.</li><li>Delacroix concluded that music training may sharpen listening skills.</li></ul><p>The student wants to describe how the study was conducted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Delacroix tested children's ability to pick out sounds in noise before and after two years of music lessons.","Delacroix concluded that music training may sharpen listening skills.","Delacroix found that children who took lessons improved more than those who did not.","Music researcher Beatriz Delacroix set out to learn whether learning an instrument improves children's listening skills."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It explains the procedure. The others give the study's aim, finding, or conclusion."}
